From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nuubOS: apply the panel orientation of built-in panels

The RG28XX panel is 480x640 mounted sideways; its device tree rotation
reaches the DRM connector as "panel orientation", which wlroots maps to
an output transform (wlr_drm_connector_get_panel_orientation) but labwc
never applied. Set it when a DRM output is enabled, and draw the
first-frame boot splash (patch 0001) at the logical size.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [nuubOS specific]

--- a/src/output.c
+++ b/src/output.c
@@ -582,6 +582,17 @@
 
 	int width = mode->width;
 	int height = mode->height;
+
+	/* A panel mounted sideways (RG28XX) is drawn through the output
+	 * transform: the splash buffer has the logical size. */
+	enum wl_output_transform transform =
+		(output->pending.committed & WLR_OUTPUT_STATE_TRANSFORM)
+		? output->pending.transform : wlr_output->transform;
+	if (transform % 2) {
+		int swap = width;
+		width = height;
+		height = swap;
+	}
 	uint32_t *pixels = malloc((size_t)width * (size_t)height * 4);
 
 	if (!pixels) {
@@ -628,6 +639,21 @@
 	wlr_log(WLR_DEBUG, "enable output %s", wlr_output->name);
 	wlr_output_state_set_enabled(&output->pending, true);
 
+	/*
+	 * nuubOS: built-in panels mounted sideways or upside down (RG28XX:
+	 * 480x640 panel, device tree rotation) report it in the connector's
+	 * "panel orientation"; wlroots maps it, labwc never applied it.
+	 */
+	if (wlr_output_is_drm(wlr_output)) {
+		enum wl_output_transform transform =
+			wlr_drm_connector_get_panel_orientation(wlr_output);
+		if (transform != WL_OUTPUT_TRANSFORM_NORMAL) {
+			wlr_output_state_set_transform(&output->pending, transform);
+			wlr_log(WLR_INFO, "nuubOS: output %s panel orientation transform %d",
+				wlr_output->name, transform);
+		}
+	}
+
 	if (!output_test_auto(wlr_output, &output->pending,
 			/* is_client_request */ false)) {
 		wlr_log(WLR_INFO, "mode test failed for output %s",
